426 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (To improve interpretability, the neural network can be combined with a more explainable model such as a decision tree. For example, the neural network can be used for accurate predictions, while a decision tree can be used alongside it to provide simple, human-readable rules that help explain the results.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
427 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 97 0 R
/T (2.Limited Model Complexity)
/E (2.Limited Model Complexity)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
428 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (In this project, we used a simple neural network with only one hidden layer. While this structure is efficient and easy to train, it may not be powerful enough to capture more complex and subtle patterns in user behavior.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
429 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (Smartphone addiction is influenced by multiple interacting factors \(such as screen time, sleep, stress, and app usage\), and some of these relationships can be highly non-linear. A simple model may only learn the most obvious patterns \(like high screen time\), while missing deeper interactions between features.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
430 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E ( As a result, the model may not fully exploit all the information available in the data.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
431 0 obj
<<
